# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, which rewrites LF to CRLF
# on checkout for anything it decides is text. It decides by looking for a NUL
# byte near the start of the file -- and a PDF begins with "%PDF-1.4" and a
# stretch of ASCII, so every PDF in docs/ was being classified as text.
#
# The stored blobs were fine; the damage happened on the way out. A fresh clone
# got PDFs 200-2400 bytes larger than the originals, with a CR injected before
# every LF and every byte offset in the xref table therefore wrong. Tolerant
# readers repair them silently, which is why this went unnoticed -- strict ones
# report a broken file.
#
# The .onnx voices were never affected: protobuf has a NUL early enough for the
# heuristic to catch it. Marked anyway rather than relying on that.
*.pdf   binary
*.onnx  binary
*.db    binary

# Everything else can be normalised to LF in the repository as usual.
* text=auto
